  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "A first-level model may contain several\nexplanatory variables, but a scientific",
      "startSeconds": 0,
      "endSeconds": 4.800009,
      "startFrame": 0,
      "endFrame": 145
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "result begins with a focused question.",
      "startSeconds": 4.800009,
      "endSeconds": 7.418195727272727,
      "startFrame": 144,
      "endFrame": 223
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "Was the response during left-button trials\ngreater than the response during",
      "startSeconds": 7.418195727272727,
      "endSeconds": 12.218204727272727,
      "startFrame": 222,
      "endFrame": 367
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "right-button trials?",
      "startSeconds": 12.218204727272727,
      "endSeconds": 13.090933636363637,
      "startFrame": 366,
      "endFrame": 393
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "A contrast turns that comparison into\nprecise weights.",
      "startSeconds": 13.090933636363637,
      "endSeconds": 16.581849272727272,
      "startFrame": 392,
      "endFrame": 498
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "Those weights must agree with the model\ncolumns and with the words used to",
      "startSeconds": 16.581849272727272,
      "endSeconds": 22.690951636363636,
      "startFrame": 497,
      "endFrame": 681
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "describe the hypothesis.",
      "startSeconds": 22.690951636363636,
      "endSeconds": 24.000045,
      "startFrame": 680,
      "endFrame": 721
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "text": "At each voxel, FEAT fits the general\nlinear model.",
      "startSeconds": 24.850045,
      "endSeconds": 28.902559240000002,
      "startFrame": 745,
      "endFrame": 868
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "text": "The design matrix contains explanatory\nvariables, and beta contains one fitted",
      "startSeconds": 28.902559240000002,
      "endSeconds": 33.8556322,
      "startFrame": 867,
      "endFrame": 1016
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "text": "coefficient for each model column.",
      "startSeconds": 33.8556322,
      "endSeconds": 36.107029000000004,
      "startFrame": 1015,
      "endFrame": 1084
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "text": "A contrast does not change those\nestimates.",
      "startSeconds": 36.107029000000004,
      "endSeconds": 39.258984520000006,
      "startFrame": 1083,
      "endFrame": 1178
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "text": "It defines a linear combination, written\nas c transpose beta, where c is the vector",
      "startSeconds": 39.25898452,
      "endSeconds": 46.01317492,
      "startFrame": 1177,
      "endFrame": 1381
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "text": "of hypothesis weights.",
      "startSeconds": 46.01317492,
      "endSeconds": 47.364013,
      "startFrame": 1380,
      "endFrame": 1421
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "text": "Suppose the explanatory-variable order is\nLeft followed by Right.",
      "startSeconds": 48.214013,
      "endSeconds": 52.272699265625,
      "startFrame": 1446,
      "endFrame": 1569
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "text": "The weights one, zero select the Left\ncoefficient.",
      "startSeconds": 52.272699265625,
      "endSeconds": 55.880420390625,
      "startFrame": 1568,
      "endFrame": 1677
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "text": "Zero, one select the Right coefficient.",
      "startSeconds": 55.880420390625005,
      "endSeconds": 58.58621123437501,
      "startFrame": 1676,
      "endFrame": 1758
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "text": "In a usual task model, each is tested\nrelative to the implicit baseline",
      "startSeconds": 58.586211234375,
      "endSeconds": 64.4487580625,
      "startFrame": 1757,
      "endFrame": 1934
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "text": "represented by the rest of the model.",
      "startSeconds": 64.4487580625,
      "endSeconds": 67.605514046875,
      "startFrame": 1933,
      "endFrame": 2029
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "text": "Neither is a direct Left-versus-Right\ncomparison.",
      "startSeconds": 67.605514046875,
      "endSeconds": 70.311304890625,
      "startFrame": 2028,
      "endFrame": 2110
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "text": "One, one tests their positive sum, while\none half, one half tests the numerical",
      "startSeconds": 70.311304890625,
      "endSeconds": 76.62481685937499,
      "startFrame": 2109,
      "endFrame": 2299
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "text": "average.",
      "startSeconds": 76.624816859375,
      "endSeconds": 77.075782,
      "startFrame": 2298,
      "endFrame": 2313
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "text": "To compare Left directly with Right, use\none, negative one.",
      "startSeconds": 77.925782,
      "endSeconds": 82.34402520754716,
      "startFrame": 2337,
      "endFrame": 2471
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "text": "This computes beta Left minus beta Right\nand tests the positive direction, Left",
      "startSeconds": 82.34402520754716,
      "endSeconds": 88.08774137735848,
      "startFrame": 2470,
      "endFrame": 2643
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "text": "greater than Right.",
      "startSeconds": 88.0877413773585,
      "endSeconds": 89.41321433962266,
      "startFrame": 2642,
      "endFrame": 2683
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "text": "Reversing the signs tests Right greater\nthan Left.",
      "startSeconds": 89.41321433962264,
      "endSeconds": 92.94780890566038,
      "startFrame": 2682,
      "endFrame": 2789
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "text": "A negative weight means that a coefficient\nis subtracted in this hypothesis.",
      "startSeconds": 92.94780890566038,
      "endSeconds": 98.24970075471698,
      "startFrame": 2788,
      "endFrame": 2948
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "text": "It does not, by itself, mean deactivation.",
      "startSeconds": 98.24970075471698,
      "endSeconds": 101.342471,
      "startFrame": 2947,
      "endFrame": 3041
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "text": "Contrast numbers only have meaning when\naligned with the correct design-matrix",
      "startSeconds": 102.192471,
      "endSeconds": 106.50995853333333,
      "startFrame": 3065,
      "endFrame": 3196
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "text": "columns.",
      "startSeconds": 106.50995853333333,
      "endSeconds": 106.9024574,
      "startFrame": 3195,
      "endFrame": 3208
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "text": "If the actual order is Right then Left,\none, negative one tests Right greater than",
      "startSeconds": 106.9024574,
      "endSeconds": 112.7899404,
      "startFrame": 3207,
      "endFrame": 3384
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "text": "Left, even if the contrast is named Left\ngreater than Right.",
      "startSeconds": 112.78994039999999,
      "endSeconds": 117.10742793333333,
      "startFrame": 3383,
      "endFrame": 3514
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "text": "Write the EV order, read each contrast as\na sentence, and point from every weight to",
      "startSeconds": 117.10742793333333,
      "endSeconds": 123.38740979999999,
      "startFrame": 3513,
      "endFrame": 3702
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "text": "its displayed column before running FEAT.",
      "startSeconds": 123.3874098,
      "endSeconds": 125.742403,
      "startFrame": 3701,
      "endFrame": 3773
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "text": "In FEAT, open Full model setup, then\nContrasts and F-tests.",
      "startSeconds": 126.59240299999999,
      "endSeconds": 130.90190934615384,
      "startFrame": 3797,
      "endFrame": 3928
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "text": "Give each contrast a scientific name,\nenter weights in the displayed EV order,",
      "startSeconds": 130.90190934615384,
      "endSeconds": 136.50426759615385,
      "startFrame": 3927,
      "endFrame": 4096
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "text": "and inspect the arrows in the design\npreview.",
      "startSeconds": 136.50426759615385,
      "endSeconds": 139.95187267307693,
      "startFrame": 4095,
      "endFrame": 4199
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "text": "Before selecting Done, compare every row\nwith the analysis plan and save the design",
      "startSeconds": 139.9518726730769,
      "endSeconds": 145.9851815576923,
      "startFrame": 4198,
      "endFrame": 4380
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "text": "file so the model specification remains\nreproducible.",
      "startSeconds": 145.9851815576923,
      "endSeconds": 149.001836,
      "startFrame": 4379,
      "endFrame": 4471
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "text": "For each contrast, FEAT writes several\nrelated outputs.",
      "startSeconds": 149.851836,
      "endSeconds": 153.38008167272727,
      "startFrame": 4495,
      "endFrame": 4602
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "text": "The cope is the weighted contrast estimate\nin model units.",
      "startSeconds": 153.38008167272727,
      "endSeconds": 157.79038876363637,
      "startFrame": 4601,
      "endFrame": 4734
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "text": "The varcope quantifies uncertainty in that\nestimate.",
      "startSeconds": 157.79038876363634,
      "endSeconds": 160.8776037272727,
      "startFrame": 4733,
      "endFrame": 4827
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "text": "A t statistic compares the cope with its\nstandard error, and FEAT converts it to a",
      "startSeconds": 160.8776037272727,
      "endSeconds": 167.93409507272725,
      "startFrame": 4826,
      "endFrame": 5039
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "text": "z statistic for inference.",
      "startSeconds": 167.93409507272727,
      "endSeconds": 169.6982179090909,
      "startFrame": 5038,
      "endFrame": 5091
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "text": "A z-statistic map is standardized\nevidence, not an effect-size map.",
      "startSeconds": 169.69821790909089,
      "endSeconds": 174.108525,
      "startFrame": 5090,
      "endFrame": 5224
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "text": "Before running FEAT, list the EVs in\nmatrix order and state the scientific",
      "startSeconds": 174.958525,
      "endSeconds": 180.9553042857143,
      "startFrame": 5248,
      "endFrame": 5429
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "text": "question for every contrast.",
      "startSeconds": 180.9553042857143,
      "endSeconds": 182.80046714285717,
      "startFrame": 5428,
      "endFrame": 5485
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "text": "Translate the sentence into weights, then\ntranslate the weights back into a",
      "startSeconds": 182.80046714285714,
      "endSeconds": 188.33595571428572,
      "startFrame": 5484,
      "endFrame": 5651
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "text": "sentence.",
      "startSeconds": 188.33595571428572,
      "endSeconds": 188.79724642857144,
      "startFrame": 5650,
      "endFrame": 5664
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "text": "Inspect the design matrix and contrast\narrows.",
      "startSeconds": 188.79724642857144,
      "endSeconds": 192.02628142857145,
      "startFrame": 5663,
      "endFrame": 5761
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "text": "Finally, distinguish the effect estimate,\nits uncertainty, and the standardized",
      "startSeconds": 192.02628142857145,
      "endSeconds": 196.6391885714286,
      "startFrame": 5760,
      "endFrame": 5900
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "text": "statistic.",
      "startSeconds": 196.63918857142858,
      "endSeconds": 197.1004792857143,
      "startFrame": 5899,
      "endFrame": 5914
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "text": "The model is ready when the design,\nweights, and scientific language tell the",
      "startSeconds": 197.1004792857143,
      "endSeconds": 203.0972585714286,
      "startFrame": 5913,
      "endFrame": 6093
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "text": "same story.",
      "startSeconds": 203.09725857142857,
      "endSeconds": 204.01984,
      "startFrame": 6092,
      "endFrame": 6121
    }
  ]
}
